      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Two routes. (a) CH3OH (15 mL), LiOH·H2O (0.1 mmol, 0.0042 g), and H L-pyra (0.1 mmol, 0.0257 g) were stirred, then Dy(CH3COO)3·4H2O (0.1 mmol, 0.0412 g) was added and stirred at room temperature for 0.5 h. The orange solution was filtered, sealed, and slowly evaporated at room temperature; crystals were collected after about a week (yield 40% based on DyIII salt). (b) H L-pyra (0.1 mmol, 0.0257 g) and Dy(CH3COO)3·4H2O (0.1 mmol, 0.0412 g) were dissolved in 9 mL of CH3OH/H2O (2:1), placed in a Teflon-lined autoclave, and reacted at 95 °C for 72 h to give orange crystals (yield 20% based on DyIII salt). PXRD indicated higher purity for method (a).",
        "reagents": [
